Sat Oct 17 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - tokajer <tokajer@tokajer.at>

- Keyboard: the live session now follows the chosen layout.
  nazoos-installer starts systemd-localed and keeps it running
  (Calamares does not D-Bus-activate it, localed quits after 30 s);
  keyboard.conf sets useLocale1 explicitly
- Language: nazoos-postinstall requests the installer's language for
  zypper (addlocale --no-packages), later installs get translations
- License page: disclaimer text wraps instead of being cut off
  (stylesheet qproperty-wordWrap); Calamares' header "will install
  proprietary software" hidden (wrong for the disclaimer, not configurable)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Oct 16 20:45:00 UTC 2026 - tokajer <tokajer@tokajer.at>

- nazoos-postinstall: the keyboard chosen in the installer reached
  only the text console. systemd >= 258 keeps the desktop layout in
  /etc/vconsole.conf (XKBLAYOUT), Calamares writes it to
  xorg.conf.d/00-keyboard.conf, so the image's German layout stayed on
  the desktop and login screen. The layout is now copied over, model
  pc105 instead of the image's microsoftpro, console keymap derived
  from layout+variant (German gave the Mac keymap before)
- Partitions: "Encrypt system" offered (ADR 0006). LUKS1 so GRUB can
  open it; /boot stays inside the encrypted root
- nazoos-postinstall: GRUB_ENABLE_CRYPTODISK when / is on dm-crypt.
  openSUSE's grub2 turns /etc/crypttab into crypttab_entry and hands
  the key to the initrd: the passphrase is asked once, also when
  booting a snapshot (tested with Secure Boot)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Oct 16 19:00:00 UTC 2026 - tokajer <tokajer@tokajer.at>

- Start page: minimum RAM 3.5 GiB instead of 4.0. Calamares compares
  with MemTotal, which is lower than the installed RAM (firmware and
  kernel reservations): PCs with 4 GB were refused

